 * Q: How long do seamless gutters last?
 * A: With proper maintenance, seamless aluminum gutters last 20-30 years in North Alabama's climate.
 *
 * Q: What size gutters do I need for my home?
 * A: Most homes use 5-inch K-style gutters. Homes with large roofs or steep pitches may need 6-inch gutters.
 *
 * Q: Are seamless gutters worth the investment?
 * A: Yes. Seamless gutters have fewer leak points and require less maintenance than sectional gutters.
 *
 * GUTTER GUARDS:
 * Q: Do gutter guards work with pine needles?
 * A: Quality micro-mesh guards handle pine needles well, though some surface maintenance may still be needed.
 *
 * Q: Will gutter guards void my roof warranty?
 * A: Our installation method doesn't lift shingles or void warranties. We're careful to protect your roof.
 *
 * GUTTER CLEANING:
 * Q: How often should I clean my gutters in {{CITY_NAME}}?
 * A: We recommend twice yearly - after pine needle season (October) and after leaf drop (December).
 *
 * Q: What happens if I don't clean my gutters?
 * A: Clogged gutters cause water overflow, foundation damage, fascia rot, and can attract pests.
